From: WXbet <57314510+WXbet@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: add MIPS to the Linux cacheline fallback

TORRENT_CHECK_CACHELINE first tries to read SMP_CACHE_BYTES from linux/cache.h.
That header is kernel internal and not part of the exported UAPI, so the test
never succeeds when cross compiling against a sysroot - every architecture ends
up in the CPU fallback below it. MIPS is missing from that list, so the build
aborts with "Unrecognized CPU architecture (mipsel) on Linux fallback path"
while x86 and ARM silently pick their value.

32 bytes is the L1 cacheline of the MIPS32 cores in use here.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
diff --git a/scripts/common.m4 b/scripts/common.m4
index 2d42209..9453b24 100644
--- a/scripts/common.m4
+++ b/scripts/common.m4
@@ -126,6 +126,10 @@ AC_DEFUN([TORRENT_CHECK_CACHELINE], [
             AC_MSG_RESULT([linux fallback LoongArch 64 bytes])
             AC_DEFINE([LT_SMP_CACHE_BYTES], 64, [Fallback 64-byte alignment for Linux LoongArch hardware.])
             ;;
+          mips*)
+            AC_MSG_RESULT([linux fallback MIPS 32 bytes])
+            AC_DEFINE([LT_SMP_CACHE_BYTES], 32, [Fallback 32-byte alignment for Linux MIPS hardware.])
+            ;;
           *)
             AC_MSG_RESULT([unrecognized CPU arch on Linux header fallback])
             AC_MSG_FAILURE([Unrecognized CPU architecture ($host_cpu) on Linux fallback path. Aborting build.])
